Z||000000||fropuff||09-19-2000||09:23 PM||||Hey, I'm going to have my Cutlass in the shop this weekend, so I thought that I'd do something to the Fiero.  Since the temperature gauge didn't work out (did in the Cutlass; got it in tonight) I thought I'd install my e-brake cables this weekend.  I am not a Fiero mechanic quite yet, so I need a little help.  I have no idea where to start.  I have the 4-piece kit from Dave, so I think that's all it takes.  I need a step-by-step description on how to do this.  After my cables are done, not much is left.  Let's see: ground FX painted, windshield, tires, brake pads, right side mirror glass.  I think that's it!  Sure am glad!  Oh, thanks for the help!    ||||reg||4
Z||000001||fropuff||09-20-2000||10:41 PM||||Please!  I really, really, REALLY need help.  Really.  I'm sure that someone out there has changed their e-brake cables.  (You know who I'm talking to...)  So, the Cutlass isn't going to be in the shop this weekend, but I can't really do anything to that.  E-brake cables are the only thing I've got!!!  Sure, I could take a break for the weekend, but I won't get ANYTHING done.  I'm on a limited schedule.  I've only got 'till February!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Actually, I've got 'till May for the Fiero, but I'd rather spend my time with the Fiero.  I can tell that it's sad by all the neglect it's had lately.  I've got to cheer it up.  And, the only way I can do it, is if I put my cables on............<BR>Thanks.||||reg||1
